# Chaos Destruction Performance Learning

Date: 2026-08-05

Target: Unreal Engine 5.6.1, `MCPGameProject`, UnrealMCP authoring and
verification tooling.

Status: verification complete; awaiting final Ieta audit. Initial Ieta review classified the original seven learning topics as
`BLOCKED` because the engine supports the features but the repository did not
yet contain Chaos-specific MCP commands, controlled fixtures, or numeric live
evidence. On 2026-08-05 the user explicitly removed Nanite
from the learning and test scope; completion therefore covers six topics.

## Scope

The learning loop covers all of the following:

1. Tiny Geometry merging.
2. Remove on Sleep and Remove on Break.
3. One-Way Interaction.
4. Cluster-break and released-particle throttling.
5. Native trace plus External Strain and breaking velocity.
6. Chaos Cache recording and deterministic playback.

The authoritative engine is the installed UE 5.6.1 build. When documentation
wording differs from the installed source, record the difference and use the
installed source behavior for the verdict.

## Safety Boundary

- Keep generated fixtures under `/Game/_MCP_Temp/ChaosDestructionLearning`.
- Do not modify marketplace, engine, original project, or production assets.
- UnrealMCP C++ may author and inspect assets, but generated content must not
  serialize UnrealMCP classes, functions, components, or module references.
- Do not create project C++ or gameplay/runtime helper modules.
- Preserve shared editor state. Use a separate test editor port for lifecycle,
  map-switch, PIE/SIE, cache-recording, or cleanup work.
- Scope every changed Chaos CVar and restore its previous value even on error.

## Common Verdict Rule

- `PASS`: UE 5.6.1 live PIE reaches the decisive condition and records numeric
  evidence. Performance comparisons use the same fixture, map, camera, warmup,
  and fixed-step conditions for five runs, with median and p95 reported.
- `FAIL`: the decisive condition ran, but the functional result, state change,
  limit, determinism, or expected A/B direction was wrong.
- `BLOCKED`: tooling, plugin, editor, or fixture setup prevented the decisive
  condition from running. A visual impression is never sufficient for `PASS`.

## Ieta Acceptance Matrix

### Tiny Geometry

- Start with at least 64 leaf bones and at least 12 candidates below relative
  volume `0.04`.
- After optimization, leaf/rigid-body count and peak active-body count must
  decrease, and candidates must merge into valid connected neighbors.
- Overall bounds and volume deviation must stay within one percent.
- `STAT_AdvanceClustering` median must not regress by more than five percent.

### Remove on Sleep and Remove on Break

- Exercise both mechanisms independently.
- Small pieces must be removed within one fixed tick of their configured
  completion time while designated large structural pieces remain.
- Record configured timers and per-frame active, disabled, visible, broken,
  and remaining-transform counts.

### One-Way Interaction

- Compare `OneWayInteractionLevel=-1` with level `2` using identical debris and
  a 50 kg dynamic witness body.
- The normal case must move the witness by at least one centimeter. The
  one-way case must keep witness displacement or velocity change below ten
  percent of the normal case while debris still collides with the static floor.

### Break and Particle Throttling

- Break at least eight collections in the same frame.
- With `PerAdvanceBreaksAllowed=2`, no frame may process more than two cluster
  breaks; remaining work must be observed on later frames rather than lost.
- Compare particle-release min/max throttling against the baseline and record
  per-frame break, released, active, and disabled counts.
- Restore all CVars after every run.

### Trace and External Strain

- The native trace must return actor, component, and a valid `FHitResult.Item`.
- Twenty valid hits must target the intended pieces; misses must not fracture.
- Breaking velocity must point along the requested shot direction.
- Compare 100 trace/external-strain hits with the equivalent Field path using
  five-run GameThread and Chaos timing evidence.

### Chaos Cache

- Record at least one second and at least 30 frames.
- Quantize transforms to `0.1 cm` and `0.1 degree`, then compare hashes at
  0.25, 0.5, and 1.0 seconds over two playback passes.
- Playback hashes must match, live simulation must not run in parallel with
  playback, and a 16-instance playback comparison must reduce Chaos physics
  median relative to live simulation.

## Required Tooling Surface

The first maintained command group should provide:

- `create_chaos_destruction_learning_fixture`
- `inspect_geometry_collection_performance_guarded`
- `run_chaos_destruction_performance_smoke`
- `run_chaos_cache_smoke`

The native layer is justified because UE 5.6 Unreal Python does not provide a
stable complete route for Fracture Engine Tiny Geo mutation, managed-array
removal facades, exact trace item indices, dynamic collection particle state,
or cache frame/duration evidence.

## Final Completion Gate

Learning is complete only when:

- all six in-scope topics are `PASS`, with zero `FAIL` or `BLOCKED` results;
- UE 5.6.1 build, Python compilation/import, F821, registration, response
  schema where applicable, and live bridge smokes pass;
- all performance comparisons contain five-run median and p95 evidence;
- every scoped CVar is restored;
- temporary asset and dirty-package state is reported;
- dependency audit finds no UnrealMCP/MCP-only reference in generated assets;
- the complete six-topic regression passes again after the last fix.

## Final38 Verification Results

All measurements used UE 5.6.1, an isolated editor on port `55562`, fixed
30 Hz stepping, fresh PIE per functional scenario and performance run, and the
same learning map. Nanite is `N/A`; the cinematic workflow verifies the
non-Nanite `UGeometryCollectionRootProxyRenderer` path separately.

| In-scope area | Five-run result | Verdict |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Tiny Geometry | rigid/peak active bodies `3072 -> 2304`; `STAT_AdvanceClustering` median `2.978 -> 1.609 ms`, p95 `3.715 -> 2.244 ms`; rigid pieces `96 -> 72`, candidates `24 -> 0`, volume/bounds delta `0%` | PASS |
| Remove on Sleep / Break | both mechanisms `5/5`; 24 target pieces removed and 8 designated large pieces remained in every run; representative completion delays `1.5333 s` Sleep and `0.9667 s` Break | PASS |
| One-Way Interaction | normal witness median/p95 `511.351/511.351 cm`; level-2 median/p95 `0.984/0.984 cm`, ratio `0.192%`; both paths had same-solver pair/current/enabled constraints, four manifold points, observed Phi, finite positive solver impulse, exact leaf capture, and floor reach | PASS |
| Break/Particle Throttling | `5/5`; eight simultaneous collections processed with maximum two new cluster breaks per frame; later-frame rescheduling observed and solver settings restored | PASS |
| Trace + External Strain | `100/100` valid item hits and `100/100` Field dispatches in every run; Trace median/p95 `0.404/0.524 ms`, Field median/p95 `0.462/1.000 ms` | PASS |
| Chaos Cache | deterministic two-pass hashes at 0.25/0.5/1.0 s, hashes vary across times, 1.2 s and 36+ frames, 1680 forced-kinematic physics objects, source asset not dirtied; live/playback Chaos median `2.069 -> 1.614 ms`, p95 `2.669 -> 2.122 ms` | PASS |

